        "concept": "Build a recursive CTE anchored at `manager_id IS NULL` and iteratively join direct reports up to depth 5.",
        "instructions": "Complete the `WITH RECURSIVE org_tree` query in `query.sql` to compute `hierarchy_level` and `reporting_chain`.",
        "hint": "-- Step 2 Solution (build-sessionization-retention-engine): Full WITH RECURSIVE chain-of-command traversal\nWITH RECURSIVE org_tree AS (\n  SELECT\n    emp_id,\n    name,\n    title,\n    manager_id,\n    dept_id,\n    salary_usd,\n    0 AS hierarchy_level,\n    name AS reporting_chain\n  FROM employees\n  WHERE manager_id IS NULL\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT\n    e.emp_id,\n    e.name,\n    e.title,\n    e.manager_id,\n    e.dept_id,\n    e.salary_usd,\n    t.hierarchy_level + 1 AS hierarchy_level,\n    t.reporting_chain || ' -> ' || e.name AS reporting_chain\n  FROM employees AS e\n  INNER JOIN org_tree AS t\n    ON e.manager_id = t.emp_id\n  WHERE t.hierarchy_level < 5\n)\nSELECT\n  emp_id,\n  name,\n  title,\n  hierarchy_level,\n  salary_usd,\n  reporting_chain\nFROM org_tree\nORDER BY hierarchy_level ASC, salary_usd DESC;",
        "file": "query.sql",
        "targetFile": "query.sql",
        "starterCode": "-- Step 2 Starter (build-sessionization-retention-engine): Anchor member of organizational hierarchy\nSELECT\n  emp_id,\n  name,\n  title,\n  dept_id,\n  0 AS hierarchy_level\nFROM employees\nWHERE manager_id IS NULL;",
        "solutionCode": "-- Step 2 Solution (build-sessionization-retention-engine): Full WITH RECURSIVE chain-of-command traversal\nWITH RECURSIVE org_tree AS (\n  SELECT\n    emp_id,\n    name,\n    title,\n    manager_id,\n    dept_id,\n    salary_usd,\n    0 AS hierarchy_level,\n    name AS reporting_chain\n  FROM employees\n  WHERE manager_id IS NULL\n  UNION ALL\n  SELECT\n    e.emp_id,\n    e.name,\n    e.title,\n    e.manager_id,\n    e.dept_id,\n    e.salary_usd,\n    t.hierarchy_level + 1 AS hierarchy_level,\n    t.reporting_chain || ' -> ' || e.name AS reporting_chain\n  FROM employees AS e\n  INNER JOIN org_tree AS t\n    ON e.manager_id = t.emp_id\n  WHERE t.hierarchy_level < 5\n)\nSELECT\n  emp_id,\n  name,\n  title,\n  hierarchy_level,\n  salary_usd,\n  reporting_chain\nFROM org_tree\nORDER BY hierarchy_level ASC, salary_usd DESC;"
