        "concept": "Evaluate `DENSE_RANK()`, `LAG()`, and `SUM() OVER (PARTITION BY e.dept_id ... ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW)` without collapsing employee rows.",
        "instructions": "Complete the production window query in `query.sql` and step through the Window clause in the Table Visualizer.",
        "hint": "-- Dataset: org_hr | Physical Sorting: QuickSort, Bounded Top-N Heap Sort, Incremental Sort & Disk Spills (sorting-spill-to-disk-top-n-heapsort) — Partitioned Window Ranking & Running Payroll\nSELECT\n  d.name AS dept_name,\n  e.name AS employee_name,\n  e.title,\n  e.salary_usd,\n  DENSE_RANK() OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.salary_usd DESC\n  ) AS dept_salary_rank,\n  LAG(e.salary_usd, 1, e.salary_usd) OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.salary_usd DESC\n  ) - e.salary_usd AS gap_to_higher_peer_usd,\n  SUM(e.salary_usd) OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.hired_at ASC, e.emp_id ASC\n    ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\n  ) AS cumulative_dept_payroll_usd\nFROM employees AS e\nINNER JOIN departments AS d\n  ON d.dept_id = e.dept_id\nORDER BY d.name ASC, dept_salary_rank ASC, e.emp_id ASC;",
        "file": "query.sql",
        "targetFile": "query.sql",
        "starterCode": "-- Step 3 Starter (sorting-spill-to-disk-top-n-heapsort): Departmental employee join before window frame\nSELECT\n  d.name AS dept_name,\n  e.name AS employee_name,\n  e.title,\n  e.salary_usd,\n  e.hired_at\nFROM employees AS e\nINNER JOIN departments AS d\n  ON d.dept_id = e.dept_id\nORDER BY d.name ASC, e.salary_usd DESC;",
        "solutionCode": "-- Dataset: org_hr | Physical Sorting: QuickSort, Bounded Top-N Heap Sort, Incremental Sort & Disk Spills (sorting-spill-to-disk-top-n-heapsort) — Partitioned Window Ranking & Running Payroll\nSELECT\n  d.name AS dept_name,\n  e.name AS employee_name,\n  e.title,\n  e.salary_usd,\n  DENSE_RANK() OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.salary_usd DESC\n  ) AS dept_salary_rank,\n  LAG(e.salary_usd, 1, e.salary_usd) OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.salary_usd DESC\n  ) - e.salary_usd AS gap_to_higher_peer_usd,\n  SUM(e.salary_usd) OVER (\n    PARTITION BY e.dept_id\n    ORDER BY e.hired_at ASC, e.emp_id ASC\n    ROWS BETWEEN UNBOUNDED PRECEDING AND CURRENT ROW\n  ) AS cumulative_dept_payroll_usd\nFROM employees AS e\nINNER JOIN departments AS d\n  ON d.dept_id = e.dept_id\nORDER BY d.name ASC, dept_salary_rank ASC, e.emp_id ASC;"
